---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy — OnScreenTimer" description="Privacy Policy for OnScreenTimer">
	<div class="min-h-dvh flex flex-col">
		<SiteHeader />

		<main class="flex-1 w-full max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 sm:py-20 text-zinc-800 dark:text-zinc-200">
			<div class="mb-12">
				<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-bold text-zinc-950 dark:text-zinc-50 tracking-tight mb-4">
					Privacy Policy
				</h1>
			</div>

			<article class="prose prose-zinc dark:prose-invert prose-blue max-w-none space-y-8">
				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-3">1. Overview</h2>
					<p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
						OnScreenTimer is a browser-based utility. We prioritize keeping the application lightweight and keeping your data where it belongs: in your browser.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-3">2. Information stored in your browser</h2>
					<p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed mb-3">
						To provide a seamless experience, supported application state may be stored using your browser's local storage mechanism (localStorage). This allows you to refresh the page without instantly losing your current session.
					</p>
					<p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
						This stored information includes:
					</p>
					<ul class="list-disc pl-5 mt-2 space-y-1 text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400">
						<li>Timer and Stopwatch state</li>
						<li>Tasks, task statuses, and task elapsed durations</li>
						<li>Display mode, style, and size preferences</li>
						<li>Clock format preferences</li>
						<li>Theme (light/dark) selection</li>
						<li>Sound preferences</li>
						<li>Study Block preset state</li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-3">3. Accounts</h2>
					<p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
						No account or registration is currently required for normal use of OnScreenTimer.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-3">4. Server / cloud storage</h2>
					<p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
						OnScreenTimer currently stores Timer, task, and preference state locally in your browser rather than sending that saved application state to an OnScreenTimer account or cloud-sync service. When you load the site, standard network requests are naturally made to fetch the website's files.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-3">5. Clearing local data</h2>
					<p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
						Because your application data is stored in your browser, you can remove this locally stored state at any time by clearing your browser's local storage or site data for OnScreenTimer.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-3">6. Analytics / advertising / third parties</h2>
					<p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed mb-2">
						OnScreenTimer does not currently include an advertising or analytics integration in the application.
					</p>
					<p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
						If analytics, advertising, or other data-handling services are introduced, this policy will be updated.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-3">7. Changes to this policy</h2>
					<p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
						This privacy policy may be updated as the service changes, adds features, or as regulatory requirements evolve.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-100 mb-3">8. Contact</h2>
					<p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
						If you have any questions or feedback, please visit our <a href="/contact" class="text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4">Contact page</a>.
					</p>
				</section>
			</article>
		</main>
		<SiteFooter />
	</div>
</Layout>
